# Configuration reference for AI Grand Prix
#
# READ THIS FIRST: this file is documentation, not a sourced file. Nothing in
# this project reads .env. It exists so that (a) a fork knows the real knobs,
# and (b) the .gitignore negation rule (!.env.example) has a template to keep
# tracked if someone later adds a real .env with a secret in it.
#
# There are no secrets in this project. No API keys, no cloud account, no
# tokens. Every model runs on your machine.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Shell environment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by tools/engines_up.sh only.
#
# SKIP_CLEF=1 leaves the 11 GB Clef-flash 9B model out of the startup, which
# keeps the first download at about 2.2 GB instead of 13 GB.
#
#   SKIP_CLEF=1 ./tools/engines_up.sh

SKIP_CLEF=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Command line flags (preferred over env vars)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ./run.sh [--replay] [PORT]
#   --replay   autostart two synthetic racers, needs no models at all
#   PORT       dashboard port, defaults to 8078
#
#   ./run.sh                # port 8078, nothing races until you press Start
#   ./run.sh --replay       # offline demo, no models needed
#   ./run.sh 9000           # dashboard on 9000
#
# python3 server.py --port 8078 --host 127.0.0.1 --config config.json --out runs
#
# python3 tools/run_headless.py --laps 2 --track speedway [--engines julia-1-144m,kev-0.8b]
#
# python3 tools/probe_engines.py          # ask every engine for a real decision

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Race settings
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These live in config.json, not in the environment. See the "race" block there:
#
#   laps                 2      laps that count as a finish
#   time_cap_s           240    hard stop for the whole race
#   sim_hz               60     physics and render rate
#   tick_hz              20     decisions per second per racer
#   policy               sample "sample" draws from the distribution, "argmax" takes the top
#   seed                 20261015  same seed, same race
#   decision_timeout_s   12     a racer that takes longer than this is an error, not a guess
#   track                circuit   default map
